    "chapter_name": "Center of Mass Momentum and Collision",
    "year": "2024",
    "shift": "shift_1"
  },
  "question": {
    "text": "The identical spheres each of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>M</mi></math> are placed at the corners of a right angled triangle with mutually perpendicular sides equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> each. Taking point of intersection of these two sides as origin, the magnitude of position vector of the centre of mass of the system is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow><mi>x</mi></mfrac></math>, where the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is ________."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0019_0e30d71ca868.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 199px;\"/></p><p>Position vector <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mover><mi>r</mi><mo>→</mo></mover><mi>COM</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mover><mi>r</mi><mo>→</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mover><mi>r</mi><mo>→</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mover><mi>r</mi><mo>→</mo></mover><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mo> </mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mover><mi>r</mi><mo>→</mo></mover><mtext>COM </mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>M</mi><mo>×</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>M</mi><mo>×</mo><mn>4</mn><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>M</mi><mo>×</mo><mn>4</mn><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn><mi>M</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mover><mi>r</mi><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>|</mo><mover><mi>r</mi><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>|</mo><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Therefore, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>.</p>"
  }
